# Midnight / Compact build output.
#
# DELIBERATELY COMMITTED, including the ~13 MB of prover keys under managed/.
# A teammate who recompiles with a different Compact version produces keys that
# mismatch the DEPLOYED contract's verifier keys, and the resulting proof
# rejection looks exactly like a forged credential. Shipping one known-good set
# removes that failure mode, lets anyone run the chain-service without the
# Compact toolchain, and puts the ZK assets in the Docker build context (the
# zkConfigProvider needs keys/ + zkir/ at runtime or every proof fails).
#
# compiler/contract-info.json in particular records each circuit's arguments and
# result type — exactly what the contract can reveal — so it is diffed in review
# as a privacy-surface change. See docs/smart-contract.md and docs/deployment.md.
midnight/**/build/

# Private state / witness material — NEVER commit. Credential fields and salts.
midnight/chain-service/.private-state/
.private-state/
*.vault

# Wallet-SDK local LevelDB state (sync cache / tx history) — found committed by
# accident across three earlier commits: whatever @midnight-ntwrk package opens
# this (not our own Vault, which lives under .private-state/ above) defaults to
# a relative "midnight-level-db" path when run from midnight/chain-service/, so
# every script invocation silently produced a git diff of binary DB files.
# Runtime cache, not source — never belongs in version control regardless of
# which package created it.
midnight-level-db/

# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

